  "index_test": "in-silico-only",
  "index_test_evidence": "Herein, we take a mathematical approach to delineate the mechanism underlying the human-mouse difference in radiation-related cancer risk. We used a multistage carcinogenesis model assuming a mutational action of radiation to analyze previous data on cancer mortality in the Japanese atomic bomb survivors and in lifespan mouse experiments.",
  "decision": "exclude",
  "reason": "The study uses a mathematical model (in silico) to compare human and mouse data, rather than reporting a quantitative measure of agreement based on whole-animal in vivo results predicting human outcomes. The animal data is used as input for the model, not as the index test itself."
